step.prompt:
Review the specs for this {{params.work}} ({{ticket.title}}) as the engineer who has to build it. Pass {{loop.iteration}}.

Read {{scratch.path}}/SPECS.md, and check it against {{scratch.path}}/INTENT.md and {{scratch.path}}/RESEARCH.md, and FINDINGS.md and the spike and prototype reports (*_REPORT.md) there if there are any. Do not change any files.

{{params.extra}}

Work out what would still make someone guess while building or testing it: missing behaviour, ambiguous wording, unhandled errors or edge cases, acceptance criteria that can't be checked, contradictions with the intent, the research or the code, and anything in scope that the specs don't cover. Settle what you can by reading. Ask the user about the rest: only questions that matter, each answerable on its own.

Then reply with the whole revised SPECS.md, in markdown, and nothing else. Keep its sections. If, after the answers, nothing is left that you'd need to ask, end the document with this line on its own: {{params.marker}}
Otherwise don't write that line; a further pass will pick up what's left.
